upstream: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cloudflare/skills/main/skills/web-perf
verified: 2026-09-29
scope: directory
reason: Deliberate local improvements on top of upstream (compared against upstream 3af2c774, 2026-09-05). Local keeps: a degraded no-MCP path that still does codebase/static-asset work and hands raw browser timings to ui-validation instead of stopping (design-taste, admin-dashboard, storefront-ux and ui-validation delegate here); SSH-safe MCP registration (`--headless`, global binary, headless ~780px viewport trap, `--browserUrl` attach); an explicit recorded lab profile via `emulate` (Slow 4G, 4x CPU, mobile viewport); the complementary `lighthouse_audit` (which excludes performance) routed to ui-validation for interaction claims; and a description that front-loads the ui-validation / design-taste boundary.
merged_from_upstream_2026-09-29: discover tools before starting (incl. `--slim` exposing no trace tools); change MCP configuration only within authorized scope, otherwise ask; `chrome-devtools-mcp@latest` as the upstream install path. Also merged from the chrome-devtools-mcp README/configuration/tool-reference (not in upstream skill): `--viewport`, CrUX field-data lookup and `--no-performance-crux`, `--no-usage-statistics`, and the required `pageId` on page-scoped tools.
would_lose_if_wired: A byte-for-byte refresh would replace the degraded path with a one-line "continue and state what could not be collected", drop the SSH/headless setup, the explicit lab profile, the Lighthouse a11y/SEO pass, and the ui-validation hand-off contract, and shorten the description to one without sibling boundaries.
to_vendor: Remove this marker only if upstream adopts an equivalent no-MCP degraded workflow, an explicit throttling profile, and headless setup guidance; otherwise keep as a permanent managed fork and re-diff on each refresh.
